{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>On the day.</b> Which they made for it — the makers, like ויאמר ליוסף (Genesis 48:1), את אשר כבר עשוהו (Ecclesiastes 2:12):" "<b>To enter crevices.</b> In my opinion the one [feminine form] (variant: one name) is חפרפרת, and it is the name of a bird that flies at night like a bat, and brings itself by day into a hidden place, and some say it is a bird that eats fruit at night, and they are two words:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:48.873259442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}